KG42.register("clusters-3b9e64dbb5288554741651cd",{"id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v142-d-K001","paper":"18-dlmp_analysis","label":"Low-voltage market clearing and active-power nodal pricing given TLMP","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Low-voltage market clearing and active-power nodal pricing given TLMP","market_meaning":"Given the TLMP at the corresponding transmission node, the DSO clears the low-voltage local market and determines the active-power DLMP at distribution nodes. The Caramanis et al. [4] branch additionally retains the product scope of active power, reactive power, and reserve, as well as the reserve deliverability requirements for satisfying line and voltage limits.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The joint clearing-and-pricing procedure covers [4], [7], and [11]–[14]; the three-product scope and reserve deliverability requirements belong only to the cited [4] scheme. The two scopes intersect at [4], and the product requirements cannot be generalized to the other cited schemes.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The external TLMP, the DSO clearing responsibility, and the nodal price results constitute a complete procedural candidate rule; the product chain supplements the transaction scope of one explicit branch. This boundary does not introduce the day-ahead process of M02 or the specific optimization model of M03.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the executing entity, the given price conditions, and the low-voltage clearing activity, and retains the deliverability requirements of [4]."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the active-power nodal price results of the same clearing activity."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Clarify that the [4] scheme includes an active-power product, completing the clearing scope; do not count the standalone product fact as another complete clearing rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003"],"rationale":"The same paragraph explicitly links the DSO's local clearing under a given TLMP to the determination of distribution-node active-power DLMP, supporting the assembly mapping between activity and result."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002"],"rationale":"The two Rule-Chains respectively record the active-power product of the [4] scheme and the multi-product deliverability requirements of the same low-voltage market, which are complementary in scope; the active-power product cannot represent reactive power or reserve."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003"],"rationale":"Both references point to the same local clearing function in that common procedure; the representative selection is for display only, retaining the respective conditions and results of the original Rule-Chains."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G001","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Reactive power and reserve have appeared in the frozen textual constraints, but there is not yet a corresponding approved independent product node. Proposals v141-b-g01-P001 and v141-b-g01-P002 remain pending; this Rule-Cluster completes only assembly at the level of the existing procedure.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R003::V::product.local_energy"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P001","v141-b-g01-P002"],"required_work":"Manually review the two product proposals and their scope of application; after approval, upstream should supplement the product representation while maintaining the distinction among active power, reactive power and reserve."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G002","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence on which this Rule-Cluster relies remains unverified; it has only obtained candidate-support eligibility in this experiment and has not passed independent source review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E002","v141-b-g01-E003"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently, manually check the source text, cited scheme and scope of application item by item; assembled only indicates that procedure assembly within the limited scope has been completed."}]},"rule_refs":["18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R001","18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R002","18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2bf6582a237ae8bd","COMP-851574b724899235","KG31-bdb114c095f343c4","KG40-45833afd23977831"]});
